{"id":28838,"slug":"71-fragments-of-a-chronology-of-chance","title":"71 Fragments of a Chronology of Chance","year":1994,"country":"Germany, Austria","duration":99,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28838-71-fragments-of-a-chronology-of-chance","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/4a718d381aee915959bb0c1486c9814f/xZonnHyLhEOLH61SBEY4vhuhhmsrPF_large.jpg","description":"The simultaneously random and interconnected nature of modern existence comes into harrowing focus in the despairing final installment of Michael Haneke’s trilogy. Seventy-one intricate, puzzlelike scenes survey the routines of a handful of seemingly unrelated people—including an undocumented Romanian boy living on the streets of Vienna, a couple who are desperate to adopt a child, and a college student on the edge—whose stories collide in a devastating encounter at a bank. The omnipresent drone of television news broadcasts in 71 Fragments of a Chronology of Chance underscores Haneke’s vision of a numb, dehumanizing world in which emotional estrangement can be punctured only by the shock of sudden violence.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Michael Haneke","slug":"michael-haneke"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Gabriel Cosmin Urdes","role":"Romanian boy","slug":"gabriel-cosmin-urdes"},{"actor":"Lukas Miko","role":"Max, the student","slug":"lukas-miko"},{"actor":"Otto Grümandl","role":"Tomek, the old man","slug":"otto-grumandl"},{"actor":"Anne Bennent","role":"Inge Brunner","slug":"anne-bennent"},{"actor":"Udo Samel","role":"Paul Brunner","slug":"udo-samel"},{"actor":"Branko Samarovski","role":"Hans","slug":"branko-samarovski"},{"actor":"Claudia Martini","role":"Maria","slug":"claudia-martini"},{"actor":"Georg Friedrich","role":"Bernie, the soldier","slug":"georg-friedrich"},{"actor":"Alexander Pschill","role":"Hanno","slug":"alexander-pschill"},{"actor":"Klaus Händl","role":"Gerhard","slug":"klaus-handl"},{"actor":"Corina Eder","role":"Anni","slug":"corina-ede